UPDATE companies SET description='Medical Device Innovation Corp. (MDIC) is based in Irvine, California, where it provides consulting and product development services for the medical device industry. The company focuses on accelerating ideas from concept to market through an integrated approach that spans validation, regulatory filings, and clinical trials.

MDIC offers a range of services including innovation management, ideation, intellectual property assessment, product development, design validation planning, regulatory filings (510(k), PMA, De Novo), clinical trial management, financial analysis, and supply chain setup. The firm also assists with prototyping, proof-of-concept validation, FDA design control and quality system regulation (QSR) documentation (DHF, DMR, DHR), commercial product design, manufacturing setup, and FDA validation.

Its clients include organizations needing support with FDA clearance, clinical evidence generation, cost-of-goods reduction, and intellectual property strategy.

MDIC emphasizes an integrated, roadmap-driven approach that combines strategy, project management, and regulatory expertise to help clients maximize profitability and accelerate time to market.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Innovation management", "Ideation & discovery", "User needs analysis", "Concept development", "Feasibility road-mapping", "Intellectual property assessment", "Patent research", "Claim optimization", "Design around patents", "IP audit", "Product development", "Sketching", "Prototyping", "Proof-of-concept validation", "FDA design control & QSR compliance", "DHF/DMR/DHR documentation", "Commercial product design", "Manufacturing setup", "FDA validation", "Regulatory filings (510(k), PMA, De Novo)", "Clinical trial management", "Financial analysis (ROI, cost drivers, project cost management)", "Cost of goods reduction", "Supply chain setup"], "industries": ["Medical Devices"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Integrated concept-to-market approach covering validation, regulatory filings, and clinical trials", "FDA regulatory expertise including 510(k), PMA, and De Novo pathways", "Clinical trial management and design validation planning", "Intellectual property strengthening through patent research, claim optimization, and IP audits", "Cost-of-goods reduction and supply chain setup services"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Irvine, California -> /", "Services include regulatory filings, FDA product clearance, clinical trials, cost of goods reduction, supply chain setup -> /services", "Capabilities include R&D, intellectual property assessment, product development, design validation planning, regulatory filings, clinical trials -> /", "Industry focus on medical devices -> /", "Integrated approach, roadmap development, project management -> /", "Innovation management, ideation, user needs analysis, concept development, feasibility road-map, financial analysis, intellectual property -> /services", "Product development services: sketching, prototyping, proof-of-concept validation, FDA design control & QSR, DHF/DMR/DHR, commercial product design, manufacturing setup, FDA validation -> /services", "IP services: claim optimization, design around patents, patent research, IP audit -> /services"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "In addition to innovation management and product development consulting, MDIC provides value added services based on your project needs.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='medical-device-innovation-corp' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Medical Products Laboratories, Inc. (MPL) was founded in 1936 in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. The company has operated as a contract manufacturer for nearly nine decades, though the INPUT does not specify its ownership structure or founders.

MPL provides full-service contract manufacturing and packaging for human and veterinary pharmaceuticals, medical devices, and nutritional supplements. Its capabilities span formulation development, production of liquid, semi-solid, and solid dosage forms, and a broad range of packaging formats including blisters, packets, pouches, bottles, jars, pumps, sprayers, tubes, syringes, and aerosols. The company maintains a diverse equipment fleet and adds new machinery regularly; its engineering team also fabricates custom tooling for unique packaging needs. Regulatory and compliance teams support clients from pilot scale through commercial production.

The company serves the pharmaceutical, veterinary, dietary supplement, and medical device industries, supplying both human and animal health markets. Customers range from drug and supplement brands to medical device firms seeking turnkey development and manufacturing.

MPL emphasizes its turnkey approach, covering the entire product life cycle from concept to end-stage production. It highlights exceptional value and flexibility derived from its extensive in-house equipment, continuous capital investment, custom tooling capability, and dedicated regulatory guidance.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Contract manufacturing", "Formulation development", "Liquid dosage manufacturing", "Semi-solid dosage manufacturing", "Solid dosage manufacturing", "Blister packaging", "Packet packaging", "Pouch packaging", "Bottle filling", "Jar filling", "Pump filling", "Sprayer filling", "Tube filling", "Syringe filling", "Aerosol filling", "Regulatory compliance support", "Custom tooling fabrication", "Equipment customization"], "industries": ["Pharmaceutical", "Veterinary", "Dietary supplement", "Medical device"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Blister packaging lines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Turnkey service from concept to commercial production", "Extensive in-house manufacturing and packaging equipment", "Custom tooling and equipment fabrication", "Regulatory and compliance guidance through all phases", "Nearly 90 years of industry experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1936 -> db", "Headquarters Philadelphia, Pennsylvania -> db", "Full-service contract manufacturer of human and veterinary pharmaceuticals -> db", "Offers turnkey services from concept to end-stage production -> /", "Manufactures liquid, semi-solid, solid dosage forms -> /", "Packaging options include blisters, packets, pouches, bottles, jars, pumps, sprayers, tubes, syringes, aerosols -> /", "Serves pharmaceutical, veterinary, dietary supplement, medical device industries -> /", "Provides regulatory and compliance support -> /", "Engineering team fabricates custom tooling -> /", "Nearly 90 years of experience -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "M