UPDATE companies SET description='Medicatech USA was founded in 2005 in Anaheim, California, as a manufacturer and distributor of radiographic solutions. The company began with a focus on digital radiography systems for both human medical and veterinary applications.

The company designs, develops, and manufactures a range of radiographic equipment including straight-arm and U-arm systems (MasteRad MX30, MX30C, MX40), mobile C-arms (Mini-X), flat-panel detectors (MasterX and EXPRIMER series), X-ray generators (NexGen 900 series), and portable veterinary units (ClearRay 1700, 2000, SIUI). It also develops the Voyance® image acquisition software and PACS platform, featuring the ClairVoyance™ deep-learning algorithm for bone suppression. Medicatech reports 42,785 powered facilities and 11,378 dealers served.

Medicatech serves human medical radiology, veterinary radiology, chiropractic imaging, and dental imaging markets. Its customers include hospitals, clinics, chiropractors, veterinarians, and a network of dealers across the United States.

The company emphasizes American-made manufacturing, rapid installation (under 15 minutes), US-based phone support, and custom engineering to modify products for specific clinical needs. Its stated mission is to deliver seamless, reliable radiology solutions that improve clinical efficiency and patient outcomes.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Digital radiography system design", "Radiographic equipment manufacturing", "Medical image acquisition software development", "PACS (Picture Archiving and Communication Systems) software development", "Custom engineering and product modification", "System installation and integration", "Technical support and training", "Flat panel detector manufacturing", "X-ray generator manufacturing", "Portable X-ray system manufacturing", "Fluoroscopy system manufacturing", "Mammography system manufacturing", "Veterinary radiography system manufacturing"], "industries": ["Human medical radiology", "Veterinary radiology", "Chiropractic imaging", "Dental imaging"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["MasteRad MX30", "MasteRad MX30C", "MasteRad MX40", "MasteRad MX Go", "MasteRad VX Series", "MasteRad MX40sa Straight Arm", "UA-1100 U-Arm", "Mini-X Mobile C-Arm", "MasterX 800 Series Flat Panel Detectors", "MasterX IGZO Series Flat Panel Detectors", "EXPRIMER 14x17 Wireless", "EXPRIMER 10x12 Wireless", "EXPRIMER 17x17 Tethered & Wireless", "NexGen 900 Series Generators", "Mobile & Wall-Mount Dental Generator", "Master Fluoro", "ClearRay 1700", "ClearRay 2000", "SIUI Portable X-Ray", "MasterX 801 14x17 wireless", "MasterX 802 Glassless 14x17 wireless", "MasterX 803 17x17 wireless", "MasterX 804 17x17 tethered", "MasterXDent Portable X-ray Generator", "Mammo DR Panel 1824C"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Systems designed and manufactured in the United States", "Installation completed in under 15 minutes with US-based phone support", "Engineering team customizes any product line to fit client requirements", "ClairVoyance\u2122 deep-learning algorithm suppresses bone structures without additional exposure", "FDA 510(k) clearance for Mini-X mobile C-arm"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2005 -> db", "Headquarters Anaheim, California -> db", "Manufacturer and distributor of radiographic solutions -> /", "Designs, develops, manufactures radiographic equipment and software -> /about-us", "Serves human medical and veterinary markets -> /about-us", "Product lines include MasteRad, MasterX, EXPRIMER, ClearRay, NexGen -> / and /about-us", "Custom engineering offered -> /about-us", "American-made manufacturing -> /about-us", "Installation under 15 minutes with US phone support -> /", "FDA 510(k) clearance for Mini-X -> /", "42,785 powered facilities, 11,378 dealers -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "specializing in the design, development, and manufacturing of high-performance radiographic equipment, acquisition platform, and PACS (Picture Archiving and Communication Systems) software", "founded_year": "2005", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='medicatech-usa' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Medicreations is based in Las Vegas, Nevada. The company was founded by professionals with decades of combined experience in medical aesthetics and engineering, though a specific founding year is not disclosed. The founders recognized the challenges aesthetics professionals faced—lackluster service, unreliable warranties, and devices that did not deliver consistent ROI—and set out to build a different kind of device company.

Medicreations designs and manufactures a line of energy-based aesthetic devices at its FDA-audited facility in Las Vegas. The portfolio includes the MediSpa, a seven-modality facial platform; the Velo, an air-cooled CO2 laser for resurfacing and scarring; the MediDiode, a diode laser for hair removal across all skin types; the MediYag, a dual-wavelength Q-switched Nd:YAG system for pigmentation and tattoo removal; and the MediLight, an IPL platform with five wavelength filters. The company emphasizes USA-made quality, minimal consumables, and fast treatment times.

Practitioners seeking ROI-driven technology and reliable support form the core customer base. The company highlights that its technologies power treatments for acne, anti-aging, skin tightening, pigmentation, tattoo removal, and hair removal.

Medicreations differentiates itself with a two-year warranty on every device—an uncommon promise in the industry—along with included training and ongoing support. All equipment is built in an ISO-certified, FDA-compliant facility, and the company stresses durable, USA-made construction, limited consumables, and minimal maintenance to lower operating costs for clinic owners.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO Certified','FDA-Compliant']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CO2 laser device manufacturing", "Diode laser device manufacturing", "Nd:YAG laser device manufacturing", "IPL device manufacturing", "Multi-modality facial device manufacturing", "Device training and support", "Warranty service (2-year)"], "industries": ["Medical aesthetics", "Medspa", "Dermatology", "Plastic surgery", "Aesthetic clinics"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["MediSpa", "Velo", "MediDiode", "MediYag", "MediLight"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Two-year warranty on all devices", "Manufactured in FDA-audited, ISO-certified facility in Las Vegas", "Included training and ongoing support", "Fast treatment times with minimal maintenance", "Limited consumables for lower operating costs"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Las Vegas, Nevada -> db", "Founded after decades of combined experience in medical aesthetics and engineering -> /about", "Devices manufactured in FDA-audited facility in Las Vegas -> /about", "ISO Certified, FDA-Compliant facility -> /", "Product lines: MediSpa, Velo, MediDiode, MediYag, MediLight -> /, /about", "Two-year warranty on all devices -> /about", "Included training and ongoing support -> /about", "Industries served: medical aesthetics, medspa, dermatology, plastic surgery -> /, /about", "Treatments: acne, anti-aging, skin tightening, pigmentation, tattoo removal, hair removal -> /", "USA-made quality -> /about", "Fast treatment times, minimal maintenance, limited consumables -> /, /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "All devices are manufactured in our FDA-audited facility in Las Vegas.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='medicreations' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Medway Plastics Corporation was founded in 1974 in Long Beach, California, and remains family-owned. The company operates a second facility in Pflugerville, Texas, near Austin. No founder names are disclosed in the source material.

The company specializes in custom plastic injection molding and design, offering single- and multi-cavity tooling for small, medium, and large parts. Its Long Beach plant runs 26 injection presses, 16 of which are 500 tons or larger, while the Pflugerville site operates four presses. Medway processes both commodity and engineering resins and recycles all plastic scrap back into production. A distinctive feature is its on-site electric co-generation system: three 375-kilowatt natural-gas generators with absorption chillers that supply electricity, recover heat for mold-cooling refrigeration, and provide whole-plant backup power.

The company also develops and sells proprietary products under its own brand.

Sustainability and energy independence are central to Medway''s positioning. The co-generation system has operated for roughly 11 years, and the firm has added Thermal Control Solution radiant heating systems to its largest presses to further reduce energy consumption. The company emphasizes that its sustainable processes and material choices are driven by both environmental and cost-control objectives.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom plastic injection molding", "Injection molding design", "Single-cavity and multi-cavity tooling", "Commodity resin molding", "Engineering resin molding", "Proprietary product development", "Quality assurance", "Sustainable molding processes", "Co-generation energy system operation", "Plastic scrap recycling"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Commodity resins", "Engineering resins", "Custom formulated materials"], "equipment": ["Injection molding presses (500+ ton)", "Thermal Control Solution radiant heating systems", "375-kW natural gas generators with absorption chillers", "Co-generation system (electricity, heat recovery, refrigeration)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Sustainable plastic injection molding and design since 1974", "On-site co-generation system supplying electricity, mold-cooling refrigeration, and backup power", "Full recycling of plastic scrap into production", "Family-owned with facilities in California and Texas", "Thermal Control Solution radiant heating on large-tonnage presses"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1974 -> db", "Headquarters Long Beach, California -> db", "Family-owned -> /", "Second facility in Pflugerville, Texas -> /", "26 injection presses in Long Beach, 16 at 500+ tons -> /", "4 injection presses in Pflugerville -> /", "Co-generation system with three 375-kW generators and absorption chillers -> /", "Recycles all plastic scrap -> /", "Processes commodity and engineering resins -> /", "Single- and multi-cavity configurations for small, medium, large parts -> /", "Proprietary products offered -> /", "Quality Assurance mentioned -> /", "Thermal Control Solution radiant heating systems on large presses -> /", "Sustainable Plastic Injection Molding & Design since 1974 -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We manufacture a wide range of plastic products for our customers.", "founded_year": "1974", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='medway-plastics-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Melnick Metal Works Inc. has operated from Bristol, Connecticut since its founding in 1960. The third-generation, family-owned business began as a metal fabrication shop serving the local area and has continued under family stewardship for over six decades.

The company provides custom metal fabrication across a range of processes: cutting, bending, and shaping sheet metal for prototypes and production runs; building commercial and residential kitchen hoods in stainless steel; fabricating automotive brackets, panels, and structural parts for restoration and custom builds; producing railings for stairs, safety barriers, and decorative applications; constructing metal roofs and awnings for weather protection; manufacturing industrial components such as machine parts, enclosures, and structural elements; and creating architectural metalwork including decorative panels and structural components for buildings and public spaces. The shop''s team of fabricators brings more than 100 years of combined experience to projects of varying scale.

Customers span residential, commercial, and industrial sectors. The company has supplied hoods to restaurants, railings to homes and businesses, automotive parts to classic-car restorers, and structural components to manufacturers and construction firms.

Melnick Metal Works emphasizes its experienced workforce, on-time delivery, and ability to handle jobs from small residential tasks to large industrial projects. The family-owned structure is cited as a foundation for its commitment to quality and long-term customer relationships.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom metal sheet fabrication", "Cutting, bending, and shaping metal sheets", "Commercial and residential hood fabrication", "Automotive metal component fabrication", "Custom railing fabrication", "Custom metal roof and awning fabrication", "Industrial metal component manufacturing", "Architectural metal fabrication"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Automotive", "Architectural", "Food service", "Construction", "Heavy equipment"], "materials": ["Stainless steel", "Various metals"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 100 years of combined fabricator experience", "Timely delivery without compromising quality", "Custom solutions from small residential to large industrial projects", "Third-generation family-owned since 1960", "Serving residential, commercial, and industrial sectors"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1960 -> /", "Headquarters Bristol, Connecticut -> /", "Third-generation family-owned -> /", "Over 100 years combined fabricator experience -> /", "Services: sheet metal cutting/bending/shaping -> /", "Commercial/residential hood fabrication -> /", "Automotive component fabrication -> /", "Custom railing fabrication -> /", "Custom roof and awning fabrication -> /", "Industrial component manufacturing -> /", "Architectural metal fabrication -> /", "Industries: residential, commercial, industrial, automotive, architectural, food service, construction, heavy equipment -> /", "Testimonial from New England Machine Tools -> /", "Timely delivery claim -> /", "Custom solutions claim -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We cut, bend, and shape metal sheets to match your exact needs. We design and build kitchen hoods for homes and businesses. We fabricate metal components for vehicles, including brackets, panels, and structural parts. We fabricate railings for homes, businesses, and industrial spaces. We build custom metal roofs and awnings for residential, commercial, and industrial use. We manufacture metal components and structures for industrial applications. We fabricate metal elements for buildings and outdoor spaces.", "founded_year": "1960", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='melnick-metal-works-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mercury Electronics, based in Seven Valleys, Pennsylvania, has been in continuous operation since 1946. The company provides electrical and electronic contract manufacturing services for commercial and military industries worldwide.

The company produces custom electrical and electronic assemblies including cable assemblies, wire harnesses, panel wiring, and electromechanical assemblies. Its facility handles projects from simple cut-and-stripped wire to complex control panels and enclosures. Manufacturing processes include cutting, stripping, terminating, splicing, crimping, soldering, ultrasonic welding, potting, encapsulation, wire marking, over-braiding, EMI shielding, and watertight harness assembly. The company supports prototype, low-volume, and high-volume production with just-in-time delivery.

Mercury serves industries such as defense, heavy equipment, transportation, and HVAC, primarily supplying OEM manufacturers. Its customer base spans commercial and military applications globally.

The company’s stated mission is to exceed customer expectations by delivering superior quality products on time at the lowest possible cost. It emphasizes a 100% customer satisfaction goal, backed by an engineering team averaging 31 years of experience, ISO 9001/AS9100 certification, UL recognition for wiring harnesses, and an IPC-A-620 certified trainer on staff.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','AS9100','UL Recognized for Wiring Harnesses (UL File E163115)','IPC-A-620','IPC/WHMA-A-620','DNV certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Engineering support", "Sales and estimating", "Quality inspection and testing", "Material planning", "Vendor managed inventory", "Cut, strip, and terminate", "Splicing", "Mechanical crimp", "Solder splice", "Ultrasonic welding", "Soldering", "Crimping", "Potting and encapsulation", "Wire marking", "Inline inkjet printing", "Shrink tubing", "Wraparound laminate markers", "Over-braiding", "EMI shielding and watertight harness assembly", "Automatic labeling", "Bar coding", "ESD processing", "Special packaging", "Auto bagging"], "industries": ["Defense", "Heavy equipment", "Transportation", "HVAC", "Commercial", "Military"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Automatic testing equipment (continuity, high potential, Meg Ohm)", "Custom test fixtures", "Automatic labeling equipment", "Inline inkjet printing equipment"], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production with JIT delivery", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Engineering team with average 31 years of experience", "ISO 9001 and AS9100 certified quality management system", "UL Recognized for Wiring Harnesses (UL File E163115)", "IPC-A-620 certified trainer on staff", "Vendor-managed inventory with Kanban, MIN/MAX, and bin replenishment programs"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1946 -> db", "Headquarters Seven Valleys, Pennsylvania -> db", "Contract manufacturing services for commercial and military industries -> /", "Custom electrical/electronic assemblies: cable assemblies, wire harnesses, wiring of enclosures -> /", "Processes: cut, strip, terminate, splicing, mechanical crimp, solder splice, ultrasonic welding, soldering, crimping, potting, encapsulation, wire marking, inline inkjet printing, shrink tubing, wraparound laminate markers, over-braiding, EMI shielding, watertight harness assembly, automatic labeling, bar coding, ESD processing, special packaging, auto bagging -> /services", "Engineering support with team averaging 31 years experience -> /services", "Quality: ISO 9001/AS9100 certified, UL Recognized for Wiring Harnesses (UL File E163115), IPC-A-620 standards, certified IPC-A-620 trainer -> /quality", "Industries served: defense, heavy equipment, transportation, HVAC -> /", "Volume: prototype, low-volume, high-volume with JIT delivery -> /about", "Mission: exceed customer expectations, superior quality, on time, lowest cost -> /about", "Vendor managed inventory: Kanban, bin replenishment, MIN/MAX -> /services", "Material planning capabilities -> /services", "Certified by DNV -> /quality"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are the leading provider of electrical/electronic contract manufacturing services for the commercial and military industries.", "founded_year": "1946", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mercury-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mermar Electronics is a contract electronics manufacturer based in Hesperia, California, founded in 1999. The company provides PCB fabrication, assembly, cable harness, box build, and electro-mechanical assembly services from a single facility in the High Desert region.

The company operates a state-of-the-art assembly plant capable of surface-mount, through-hole, and mixed-technology PCB assembly, including fine-pitch placement down to 01005/0201 components and BGA rework. It offers PCB fabrication, design, quick-turn prototyping as fast as 24 hours, and full box-build integration with testing, packaging, and labeling. Services cover prototype to high-volume production runs, with both consignment and turnkey material management options.

Mermar serves original equipment manufacturers in aerospace, medical, dental, therapeutic, telecommunications, industrial, renewable energy, kiosk, and guitar pedalboard markets. Its aerospace work is backed by AS9100 Rev D certification and ITAR registration, while medical assemblies follow ISO 9001:2015 and RoHS compliance.

The company emphasizes rapid turnaround, advertising same-day and next-day quick-turn assembly, 24-hour prototype builds, and a one-stop turnkey model that eliminates multi-vendor coordination. All products are built in the USA under a quality system that includes AOI, X-ray inspection, and adherence to IPC standards.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AS9100 Rev D','ITAR Registered','RoHS Compliant']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB Assembly (SMT, Through-hole, Mixed Technology)", "PCB Fabrication", "PCB Prototyping", "PCB Design & Layout (Allegro, PADS)", "Electro-Mechanical Assembly", "Box Build / System Integration", "Cable Harness Assembly", "Turnkey PCB Assembly", "Panel Mount Assembly", "PCBA Material Management", "BGA Rework & Repair", "X-Ray Inspection", "Automated Optical Inspection (AOI)", "Functional Testing", "Fine-Pitch Component Placement (01005, 0201, 0.25mm pitch)", "Leadless Component Assembly (BGA, \u00b5BGA, LGA, PoP)", "Press-Fit Connector Assembly", "Quick-Turn Assembly (Same Day, Next Day)", "Consignment (Labor-Only) Assembly", "Custom System Enclosures", "Thermal Analysis", "Power Integrity Analysis", "AMS Simulation"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Medical", "Dental", "Therapeutic", "Telecommunications", "Industrial", "Renewable Energy", "Kiosk", "Guitar Pedalboard", "Electronics (OEM)"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["BGA Rework Systems", "X-Ray Inspection Equipment", "Automated Optical Inspection (AOI) Equipment", "Wave Soldering Equipment", "Automated Pick-and-Place Machines"], "volume": "Prototype to high volume production", "lead_time": "24 hours for prototypes; same-day/next-day quick-turn available", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day and next-day quick-turn assembly", "24-hour prototype PCB assembly turnaround", "Turnkey and kitted service options", "ITAR registered and AS9100 Rev D certified for aerospace", "RoHS compliant, made in USA"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1999 -> db", "Headquarters Hesperia, California -> db, /about-us", "ISO 9001:2015, AS9100 Rev D, ITAR Registered, RoHS -> /, /about-us, /services", "Services: PCB assembly, fabrication, prototyping, design, electro-mechanical, box build, cable harness, turnkey, panel mount, material management -> /services, /capabilities", "Capabilities: SMT, through-hole, mixed, fine pitch 01005/0201, BGA rework, X-ray, AOI, quick-turn same/next day, 24-hour prototype -> /capabilities, /services", "Industries: aerospace, medical/dental/therapeutic, telecommunications, industrial, renewable energy, kiosk, guitar pedalboard -> /about-us, /", "Equipment: BGA rework systems, X-ray, AOI, wave soldering, pick-and-place -> /capabilities, /", "Differentiators: same-day/next-day, 24-hour prototype, turnkey/kitted, ITAR/AS9100, RoHS, made in USA -> /services, /capabilities, /", "Volume: prototype to high volume -> /services, /capabilities", "Lead time: 24 hours to 1 week, same-day/next-day -> /, /services"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Mer-Mar Electronics is a California based company, providing complete solution for contract manufacturing services from PCB Fabrication, PCB Assembly, Cable harnessing all the way to Box Build", "founded_year": "1999", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mermar-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Metal Fab Engineering operates from Winamac, Indiana, where it was founded in 1976 as a small fabrication shop by Paul Ezra and his wife Mary Lou.

The shop runs four automated lasers capable of cutting carbon steel up to 1 inch, stainless steel up to 3/4 inch, and aluminum up to 1/2 inch. Its forming department includes over 20 press brakes, highlighted by a 225-ton press with an 8-foot bed and a 175-ton CNC unit with 12-foot beds. Robotic and manual welding cells handle welded subassemblies and final assemblies, while an in-house powder coating line provides durable finishes for low-to-mid volume runs. The company also offers value-add engineering, CAD-based design consulting, and a domestic-first procurement service. Annual output reaches hundreds of thousands of parts.

Its customer base includes companies that require precision laser-cut components, formed brackets, welded frames, and finished assemblies delivered through a single-source supply chain.

