UPDATE companies SET description='Midwest Garment operates from La Crosse, Wisconsin, where it was founded in 1948 as Desmond''s Men''s Wear and Desmond''s Formal Wear. The business began as a regional distributor of tuxedos and, for two decades, manufactured its own vest and tie collections for the formalwear market. It continued in that role until 2003, when it shifted focus to broader textile manufacturing.

Today the company runs a commercial sewing, tailoring, and textile manufacturing operation staffed by more than 100 skilled sewers. Its capabilities span custom cutting, sewing, and tailoring, with specific processes that include single- and double-needle stitching, surge stitching, bar tacking, binding, blind hemming, sleeve setting, button covering and buttonholes, relabeling, heat-transfer labeling, fusing, strip cutting, and slitting. Production capacity ranges from prototyping and small batches to thousands of units per day.

Midwest Garment serves an array of industries requiring textile fabrication and repair, drawing on its heritage in formalwear to support customers needing custom sewn goods.

