UPDATE companies SET description='Midwest Plastics Inc., a family-owned manufacturer, was founded in 1945 and operates from a 48,000-square-foot facility in West St. Paul, Minnesota. The company has remained under family ownership since its inception, serving customers with custom and standard plastic products.

The company provides injection molding, thermoforming, and packaging services. Injection molding produces electronic housings, machine parts, gears, consumer products, medical components, hardware, and houseware items. Thermoforming capabilities cover machine covers, shrouds, blisters, clamshells, CRT bezels, printed-circuit-board storage trays, medical trays, automotive and aerospace components, and point-of-purchase displays. Packaging services include radio-frequency and heat sealing, boxing, labeling, collating, assembly, sorting, and shipping. The facility also supports prototype development for thermoformed parts.

Midwest Plastics serves the medical, automotive, aerospace, defense, energy, and telecommunications sectors. Its customer base includes the Department of Defense, the Department of Energy, and manufacturers of medical devices, electronic equipment, and consumer goods. The company also produces a line of consumer organizers, kitchen utensil drawers, garbage bag dispensers, and cutting boards sold directly through its website.

The company emphasizes end-to-end service from concept through design, manufacturing, warehousing, and distribution. Engineers review product designs and advise on material selection, focusing on quality design and cost-effective tooling. Trained operators run efficient equipment, while in-house quality-control personnel conduct frequent inspections to ensure consistency. Packaging receives special attention to meet specific customer requirements.', certifications=ARRAY['ROHS','ANSI','MIL-SPEC']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection molding", "Thermoforming", "Radio frequency sealing", "Heat sealing", "Boxing", "Labeling", "Collating", "Assembly", "Sorting", "Packaging and shipping", "Prototype development"], "industries": ["Medical Components", "Medical Trays and Parts", "Automotive and Aerospace Components", "Defense Industry", "Department of Energy (DOE)", "Department of Defense (DOD)", "Energy (See Power Generation)", "Telecommunications", "Industry Standards"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["End-to-end service from concept to distribution", "Engineering design review and material selection", "Cost-effective tooling design", "Trained operators with efficient equipment", "In-house quality control inspections"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1945 -> /about-us", "Family-owned since 1945 -> /about-us", "48,000 sq ft facility -> /about-us", "Location West St Paul, Minnesota -> /about-us", "Injection molding, thermoforming, packaging capabilities -> /", "Injection molded products: electronic housings, machine parts, gears, consumer products, medical components, hardware, houseware -> /", "Thermoformed products: machine covers, shrouds, blisters, clamshells, CRT bezels, PC board trays, medical trays, automotive/aerospace components, POP displays -> /", "Packaging services: RF sealing, heat sealing, boxing, labeling, collating, assembly, sorting, shipping -> /", "Prototype development for thermoforming -> /", "Industries served: Medical Components, Medical Trays and Parts, Automotive and Aerospace Components, Defense Industry, DOE, DOD, Energy, Telecommunications, Industry Standards -> db", "Certifications: ROHS, ANSI, MIL-SPEC -> db", "Consumer product line: organizers, kitchen utensil drawers, catch-all drawer organizers, garbage bag dispensers, under cabinet drawer and slide kit, 3rd Hand Cutting Board -> /about-us", "Engineering design review and material selection -> /about-us", "Cost-effective tooling design -> /about-us", "Trained operators with efficient equipment -> /about-us", "In-house quality control inspections -> /about-us", "Comprehensive packaging services -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Midwest Plastics is a Premier Manufacturer of Custom & Standard Plastic Products", "founded_year": "1945", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='midwest-plastics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Midwest Sheet Metal Company operates from Springfield, Missouri, in the heart of the Ozark Mountain region. The business is a second-generation, family-owned operation; Jan Davis’s father, Dave, began his career there in 1957 and owned the company for more than 25 years. Today, Chris and Jan Davis have led the firm for over 15 years, continuing a legacy of custom fabrication and machining that the company describes as spanning more than 50 years.

The shop provides a full range of metal fabrication and precision machining services. Its capabilities include custom fabrication, a full-service machine shop, precision tool and die work, prototype design and fabrication, shearing, cutting, bending, forming, punching, sawing, rolling, and welding. The facility maintains a large in-stock inventory of aluminum (including Tread Brite and colored grades), stainless steel, carbon steel, and structural shapes, and the company notes it is the area’s largest supplier of Aluminum Tread Brite. A deep bench of personnel—many with 10 to 20-plus years of tenure—supports the operation, which also houses a machine shop specializing in jigs, fixtures, special tooling, and die repair.

Midwest Sheet Metal serves customers across a variety of industries, with product lines that include racing components and custom semi-truck sunvisors.

