UPDATE companies SET description='Miller Wire Works, Inc. has operated in Birmingham, Alabama since its founding on April 1, 1949. The company began as a small shop with three employees under Charles E. Miller, producing woven wire partitions, guards, and folding gates. Now in its third generation of family ownership, the business remains privately held by the Miller family.

Today the company runs two manufacturing plants, a machine shop, and office space totaling 78,000 square feet with a workforce of over 50 people. Core manufacturing includes woven wire screens, polyurethane screens, rubber screens, and perforated plate.

The primary markets served are mining, aggregate, and pulp‑and‑paper operations, along with broader material‑handling, screening, crushing, and wear‑protection applications. Customers include quarry and mine operators, aggregate producers, and industrial facilities that require custom screen media and wear‑resistant components.

The company cites its differentiators as a strict policy of honesty and integrity, wire screens woven from the highest‑quality wire for maximum wear and impact resistance, urethane products formulated from premium raw materials to customer specifications, decades of experience in the aggregate and mining sectors, and a full‑service model that combines in‑house manufacturing with a broad distribution line.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Woven wire screen manufacturing", "Polyurethane screen manufacturing", "Rubber screen manufacturing", "Perforated plate manufacturing", "Material handling equipment distribution", "Wear liner fabrication", "Bucket protection fabrication", "Aggregate screening equipment distribution", "Crushing equipment distribution", "Conveyor belt supply", "Idler supply", "Scraper supply"], "industries": ["Mining", "Aggregate", "Pulp and paper", "Material handling", "Screening", "Crushing", "Wear protection"], "materials": ["Wire", "Polyurethane", "Rubber", "Steel", "Chromium-carbide overlay", "Cast alloy"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Strict policy of honesty and integrity", "Wire screens woven from highest\u2011quality wire for maximum wear and impact resistance", "Urethane products made from high\u2011quality raw materials to customer specifications", "Decades of experience serving aggregate and mining industries", "Full\u2011service supplier offering both manufactured and distributed products"], "facts_used": ["Founded April 1, 1949 in Birmingham, AL by Charles E. Miller -> /about-us", "Third-generation family-owned -> /about-us", "Two manufacturing plants, machine shop, offices totaling 78,000 sq ft -> /about-us", "Over 50 employees -> /about-us", "Manufactures woven wire screens, polyurethane screens, rubber screens, perforated plate -> /about-us", "Distributes conveyor belt, idlers, scrapers, loader bucket protection, cutting edges, aggregate screening and crus