UPDATE companies SET description='Minnesota Micro Molding, Machining & Manufacturing (operating as M5 Micro) was founded in 2016 in Hutchinson, Minnesota. The company began as a specialist in micro-scale molding and machining, combining both capabilities under one roof.

The shop runs micro injection molding with shot sizes from 0.0001 g to 0.6 g, processing thermoplastics and metal injection molding (MIM) materials, including overmolding, insert molding, and dual-shot (2K) operations. It also operates 5-axis micro machining on KERN Micro Vario centers with robotic pallet loading for 24/7 lights-out production, wire EDM (Mitsubishi MV1200S), small-hole EDM, and in-house metrology (Mitutoyo CMM, vision system, Starrett optical comparator). Gage-quality molds and tooling are built internally on the same 5-axis machines. The facility supports prototype through high-volume cell production.

Primary markets include medical devices (surgical tools, catheters, implant components, diagnostic cartridges, pacemaker-class parts), fiber-optic ferrules for AI compute and satellite interconnects, photonics packaging, microfluidics, drug delivery, aerospace & defense, and electronics. Customers are typically medical device OEMs and photonics manufacturers requiring tight tolerances, material traceability, and PPAP-ready documentation.

The company emphasizes its integrated "full-stack" cell: robotic part extraction, 100% in-line vision inspection every cycle, automated tray loading with per-slot traceability, and in-house heat treating and surface grinding to avoid outsourcing delays. This setup aims to deliver sub-micron repeatability and consistent unattended runs.', certifications=ARRAY['PPAP-ready','FAIR/ISIR documentation']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Micro Injection Molding", "Thermoplastics & MIM (Metal Injection Molding)", "Overmolding", "Insert Molding", "Dual-shot (2K) Molding", "5-Axis Micro Machining", "Wire EDM", "Small-Hole EDM", "Metrology & Inspection (CMM, Vision, Optical Comparator)", "Precision Toolmaking", "Surface Grinding", "Heat Treating", "Robotic Part Handling", "100% In-Line Vision Inspection", "Tray Loading & Packaging with Traceability", "FAIR/ISIR/PPAP Documentation"], "industries": ["Medical Devices", "Fiber-Optic Ferrules", "Photonics", "Microfluidics", "Drug Delivery", "Aerospace & Defense", "Electronics"], "materials": ["Thermoplastics", "Metal Injection Molding (MIM)", "Medical-grade thermoplastics", "Hardened tool steel", "Tool steels and alloys"], "equipment": ["KERN Micro Vario 5-axis machining center", "HEIDENHAIN TNC 640 control", "Mitsubishi MV1200S Wire EDM", "Mitutoyo CMM", "Mitutoyo Vision System", "Starrett Optical Comparator", "KERN Robotic Cell with internal pallet loading", "M5iE Micro Molding System"], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "Sub-micron repeatability; wire EDM to 0.001 mm; micro end mills to 0.0101 mm diameter", "built_on": ["24/7 lights-out machining with robotic pallet loading", "Sub-micron repeatability on 5-axis micro machining", "Micro injection molding shot sizes down to 0.0001 g", "In-house gage-quality mold cavities machined on KERN 5-axis", "100% in-line vision inspection with PPAP-ready traceability"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2016 in Hutchinson, Minnesota -> /", "Micro inject