UPDATE companies SET description='Minnesota Valley Electric Cooperative (MVEC) is headquartered in Jordan, Minnesota. Founded on March 6, 1937, the cooperative was formed when three small electric organizations from Carver, Le Sueur, and Scott counties merged under President Franklin D. Roosevelt’s New Deal rural electrification program. The cooperative is owned by its member-owners and operates as a not-for-profit utility.

MVEC provides electric distribution service to more than 48,500 meters across a 968-square-mile territory spanning nine Minnesota counties: Blue Earth, Carver, Dakota, Hennepin, Le Sueur, Rice, Scott, Sibley, and Waseca. The cooperative purchases wholesale power from two generation providers and maintains its own distribution infrastructure, including regular maintenance and tree-trimming programs. Notable growth milestones include the acquisition of 3,500 members from Alliant Energy in 2015 and a service-area exchange with the City of Shakopee that added 537 new services in 2022.

Its load-management programs, branded as Energy Wise, allow participants to reduce peak demand through controlled water heating, air conditioning, and smart thermostat cycling. MVEC also sponsors community initiatives such as the National Rural Electric Cooperative Association’s Youth Tour.

MVEC’s stated mission is to be a energy partner with the privilege to serve, guided by values of safety, innovation, accountability, and cooperation.', certifications=ARRAY['ENERGY STAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Start/Stop Service", "Load Management (Energy Wise)", "Outage reporting and mapping", "SmartHub online account management", "Bill payment processing", "Youth Tour sponsorship"], "industries": ["Electric power distribution", "Utilities", "Rural electrification"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Member-owned cooperative structure", "ACSI customer satisfaction award (2023\u20132026)", "Energy Wise load management programs", "Service territory spanning nine Minnesota counties"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Jordan, Minnesota -> /about-us", "Founded March 6, 1937 -> /about-us", "Formed by merger of three electric organizations under New Deal -> /about-us", "Member-owned cooperative -> /about-us", "Serves 48,500+ meters across 968 sq mi in nine counties -> /about-us", "Wholesale power from two providers -> /about-us", "Acquired 3,500 members from Alliant Energy in 2015 -> /about-us", "Added 537 services via Shakopee exchange in 2022 -> /about-us", "Energy Wise load management programs -> /", "Youth Tour sponsorship -> /", "Mission and values statements -> /about-us", "ACSI award 2023-2026 -> /about-us", "ENERGY STAR certification -> db", "Start/Stop Service capability -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Minnesota Valley Electric Cooperative (MVEC) provides reliable, affordable power to more than 48,500 meters across 968 square miles in nine Minnesota counties", "founded_year": "1937", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='minnesota-valley-electric-cooperative' AND approved AND profile I