UPDATE companies SET description='Mira Plastics Co. Inc., a family-owned plastic injection molding company, was established in 1955 in Fredon Township, New Jersey (mailing address Newton, NJ). The business began producing hobby and recreational items before expanding into a full-service molder for a broad range of industries.

The company operates a 62,000-square-foot, climate-controlled facility equipped with injection molding machines ranging from 60 to 1,250 tons, all served by robotic part removal. In addition to thermoplastic molding, Mira Plastics provides in-house 3D CAD part design, injection molding simulation analysis, and 3D prototype printing. Secondary services include ultrasonic welding (up to 2,000 watts), hot stamping (up to 15 tons), heat transfer decal application, threaded insert staking, packaging, warehousing, and distribution. The firm works with both commodity- and engineering-grade thermoplastic resins, offering resin selection expertise.

Mira Plastics serves industrial, commercial, medical, cosmetic, electronic, domestic, and food-and-beverage markets across the United States. Its customer base includes businesses in all 50 states, with the company emphasizing its ability to support projects from prototype through high-volume production.

The company highlights its solar-powered, ISO-certified facility and its family-owned heritage as key differentiators. It also stresses expertise in complex mold configurations—including two-plate, three-plate, runner-less, and hydraulic core-pull molds—and a deep knowledge of polymer rheology to optimize material selection for each project.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Thermoplastic injection molding (60\u20131,250 tons)", "Custom injection molding", "Long and short production runs", "3D CAD part design", "3D injection molding simulation analysis", "3D prototype printing", "Ultrasonic welding (up to 2,000 watts)", "Hot stamping (up to 15 tons)", "Heat transfer decal application", "Threaded insert staking", "Packaging", "Warehousing and distribution", "Decorating", "Resin selection and material consultation"], "industries": ["Industrial", "Commercial", "Medical", "Cosmetic", "Electronic", "Domestic", "Food and Beverage"], "materials": ["Commodity-grade thermoplastics", "Engineering-grade thermoplastics", "Thermoplastic polymers and resins", "Colorants", "Additives"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated since 1955", "62,000 sq ft solar-powered, climate-controlled facility", "Injection molding capacity from 60 to 1,250 tons with robotic part removal", "In-house 3D CAD design, simulation, and prototype printing", "Ultrasonic welding up to 2,000 watts and hot stamping up to 15 tons"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1955 -> db", "Family-owned -> /", "Location: Fredon Township, New Jersey -> /", "62,000 sq ft facility -> /", "Injection molding 60-1250 tons -> /", "Robotic part removal -> /", "Climate-controlled facility -> /", "Solar-powered facility -> /", "Services: 3D CAD design, simulation, prototype printing -> /", "Secondary services: ultrasonic welding, hot stamping, heat transfer decal, threaded insert staking, packaging, warehousing, shipping -> /", "Materials: commodi