UPDATE companies SET description='The company was formed in 1996 when Modern Plastics Molding (founded 1965 in Independence, Missouri) and Alpha Plastics (a Kansas City molder founded in the early 1960s) merged, combining sixty years of precision injection molding experience. Today the business is led by Anthony C. Gross, President and Chief Engineer, who oversees quoting and mold approvals directly.

The shop runs twenty-one injection molding presses ranging from 50 to 1,550 tons of clamp force, with shot capacities of 2 to 75 ounces and part weights from 5 grams to 10 pounds. Production volumes span 250 to over five million parts annually. In-house capabilities cover mold design, build, qualification, repair, and maintenance through vetted tooling partners, plus secondary operations including ultrasonic welding, CNC machining, sub-assembly, custom packaging, heat sealing, and pad printing. The company processes nine engineering-grade resin families along with commodity, glass-filled, mineral-filled, and impact-modified materials.

Modern Alpha serves aerospace and defense (ITAR-registered), medical device, drone and UAS, consumer, and industrial markets. Specific programs include structural drone brackets, legacy OEM re-engineering, metals-to-plastics conversions, thin-wall food-grade containers, and large industrial housings. Customers range from OEMs requiring close-tolerance components to firms needing turnkey design-to-distribution support.

The company emphasizes engineer-led, single-source responsibility — design, tooling, molding, assembly, and shipping under one purchase order. Statistical Process Control and Statistical Quality Control run on every press every shift, with material inspection at receiving, in-process evaluation, pre-shipping sign-off, and retained samples archived indefinitely. Long-tenured operators, some with thirty-year careers, provide tribal knowledge that the firm cites as a deliberate competitive advantage.', certifications=ARRAY['ITAR registered','ISO 9001:2015 aligned','AS9100 awareness','ISO 13485 awareness']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom injection molding", "Scientific molding", "Over-molding", "Insert molding", "Thin-wall molding", "Close-tolerance molding", "Mold design, build, and qualification", "Mold transfer and evaluation", "Mold repair and refurbishment", "Mold storage and maintenance", "Ultrasonic welding", "CNC machining and finishing", "Sub-assembly", "Custom packaging, collating, and kitting", "Heat sealing", "Pad printing", "Just-in-time (JIT) shipping", "Design engineering", "Turnkey distribution"], "industries": ["Aerospace and defense", "Medical devices", "Drone and UAS", "Consumer products", "Industrial equipment", "Food and beverage", "Legacy OEM re-engineering", "Metals-to-plastics conversion"], "materials": ["Engineering-grade resins (9 families)", "Commodity resins", "Glass-filled resins", "Mineral-filled resins", "Impact-modified resins", "Food-grade resins"], "equipment": ["21 injection molding presses (50\u20131,550 ton clamp force)", "Robotic part handling", "Computer-controlled process monitoring (SPC/SQC)", "Ultrasonic welding equipment", "CNC machining equipment", "Pad printing equipment", "Heat sealing equipment"], "volume": "250 \u2014 5,000,000+ parts annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Design. Mold. Assemble. Ship. All under one contract.", "Engineer-led, customer-first, and relentlessly hands-on ownership review of quotes and molds", "Operators with twenty- and thirty-year tenures providing tribal knowledge continuity", "ITAR registered for defense aerospace components", "Statistical Process Control and Statistical Quality Control on every press, every shift"], "facts_used": ["Formed in 1996 from merger of Modern Plastics Molding (1965) and Alpha Plastics (early 1960s) -> /about", "Headquarters at 7200 NE Birmingham Rd, Randolph, MO 64161 -> /about", "Led by Anthony C. Gross, President & Chief Engineer -> /about", "60,000 sq ft facility, 21 presses (50-1,550 ton) -> /about, /capabilities", "Part weight 5g-10lb, shot capacity 2-75 oz, volumes 250-5M+ -> /capabilities", "9 engineering-grade resin families, commodity, glass-filled, mineral-filled, impact-modified -> /capabilities", "Services: injection molding, mold building/maintenance, assembly & secondary ops (ultrasonic welding, CNC, sub-assembly, packaging, heat sealing, pad printing, JIT) -> /capabilities, /services", "Industries: drone/UAS, legacy OEM re-engineering, metals-to-plastics, medical, aerospace, consumer, industrial -> /about, /capabilities", "ITAR registered, ISO 9001:2015 aligned, AS9100 awareness, ISO 13485 awareness -> /quality", "SPC/SQC on every press every shift, four-step QC process, retained samples indefinitely -> /quality", "Engineer-led, single-source responsibility (design, mold, assemble, ship under one PO) -> /capabilities", "Operators with 20-30 year tenures, multi-generational families -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We mold for thin-wall consumer parts, close-tolerance medical components, structural drone brackets, large industrial housings, and everything in between.", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='modern-alpha-plastics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The business began as a custom metal fabrication shop serving residential and commercial projects across Northwest Arkansas and Southwest Missouri.

The company fabricates custom metal railings, including staircase, spiral staircase, and floating staircase systems, along with its proprietary Levaplate® leveling system that uses set screws to eliminate washers and shims. In-house capabilities cover welding in stainless steel, aluminum, and steel, premium powder coating on all products, and full installation services. To date, the shop has installed more than 150 custom railings.

Customers include builders and homeowners constructing or remodeling higher-end homes in Northwest Arkansas and the Joplin, Missouri area, as well as elderly clients needing handrails. The company also takes on commercial projects requiring architectural metalwork.

Modern Metal Company emphasizes a 6-to-8-week lead time, well below the industry norm of 8 to 12 months, and provides direct communication with the owner, free shop drawings, and a turnkey service from quote through installation and cleanup. The Levaplate® system and hidden-hardware design are cited as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom metal fabrication", "Welding (stainless steel, aluminum, steel)", "Powder coating", "Installation services", "Design collaboration with free shop drawings", "Levaplate\u00ae leveling system", "Custom railing fabrication (staircase, spiral staircase, floating staircase)", "In-house fabrication"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Home remodeling", "Commercial construction", "Accessibility (handrails)", "Builder/Contractor services"], "materials": ["Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Steel", "Marine-grade stainless steel", "Weather-proof wood", "Endurance powder coating", "Low-iron tempered glass"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "6 to 8 weeks", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Average lead time of 6\u20138 weeks versus an industry standard of 8\u201312 months", "Direct communication with owner Victor Onishenko throughout the project", "Free shop drawings provided during collaborative design", "Comprehensive service from initial quote to final installation and cleanup", "Proprietary Levaplate\u00ae leveling system with set screws that eliminate washers and shims"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2020 -> db", "Headquarters in Lowell, Arkansas -> db", "Owner Victor Onishenko -> /", "Custom metal railings and fabrication services -> /", "Welding in stainless steel, aluminum, and steel -> /", "Levaplate\u00ae leveling system -> /", "Powder coating on all products -> /", "Installation services -> /", "Lead time 6-8 weeks -> /", "Over 150 railings installed -> /", "Serves Northwest Arkansas and Southwest Missouri including Joplin -> /", "Free shop drawings -> /", "Direct communication with owner -> /", "Comprehensive service from quote to installation -> /", "Materials: marine-grade stainless steel, weather-proof wood, endurance powder coating, low-iron tempered glass -> /", "Free shipping on orders over $250 -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We specialize in crafting exceptional custom metal railings and providing top-notch metal fabrication services.", "founded_year": "2020", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='modern-metal-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Modern Process Equipment Corporation was founded in 1957 in Chicago, Illinois, where it maintains its worldwide headquarters. The company remains a family-owned business that has spent more than six decades designing, manufacturing, and supporting industrial process equipment for customers around the globe.

MPE builds precision particle-size-reduction equipment — including corrugated roller mills sold under the Gran-U-Lizer™ name, disc-style and roller-style coffee grinders (such as the compact SRM.MAX for espresso), and the Chain-Vey® tubular drag conveyor line for gentle, enclosed transport of bulk powders and fragile food products. The Process Systems Group integrates those machines into turnkey lines that handle classification, storage, pneumatic transport, mixing, coffee degassing, and clean-in-place automation. The company also operates grind and conveyor testing labs and runs an exchange program that restores worn rolls and heads to original condition.

The equipment serves coffee roasters (gourmet, industrial, capsule, turkish, and ultrafine), food processors (bakery, cereal, snack, peanut and tree nut, pet food), chemical and mineral producers, distilleries, breweries, and powder-and-bulk-solids handlers. Named references include Death Wish Coffee Company, Lawrence Foods, Westrock, Wicked Joe Coffee, Bird Foods, Pacifikava, a aviation supplier, a CPG brand, and a snack brand.

MPE states its purpose is to lead the invention, development, and manufacture of the industry''s most advanced processing equipment and to translate that technology into customer value through professional solutions and unwavering support — including 24/7/365 virtual assistance, global on-site service on short notice, commissioning support, and operator training.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision particle size reduction", "Corrugated roller milling (Gran-U-Lizer technology)", "Disc-style coffee grinding", "Roller-style coffee grinding", "Tubular drag conveying (Chain-Vey)", "Clean-in-place (CIP) conveyor systems", "Cable conveyor retrofit", "Process system design & integration", "Pneumatic transport", "Coffee degassing", "Grind testing lab services", "Pre-sale application analysis", "Post-sale support (phone, virtual, on-site)", "Commissioning & startup support", "Operator & maintenance training", "Spare parts supply", "Exchange program for roll/head restoration"], "industries": ["Coffee (gourmet, industrial, capsule, espresso, turkish, ultrafine)", "Food processing (bakery, cereal, snack foods, peanut & tree nuts)", "Chemical processing", "Mineral processing", "Brewery & distillery", "Pet food", "Powder & bulk solids", "Recirculating aquaculture systems", "Aviation/aerospace"], "materials": ["Coffee beans (all types)", "Food products (grains, nuts, spices, sugar, biscuits, kava root)", "Chemical products", "Minerals", "Bulk powders", "Pet food ingredients"], "equipment": ["SRM.MAX roller-style coffee grinder", "Gran-U-Lizer\u2122 precision roller mill", "Chain-Vey\u00ae tubular drag conveyor", "FCM Grinders (food, chemical, mineral)", "Industrial roller style grinders", "Gourmet disc style grinders"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Corrugated roller mill (Gran-U-Lizer\u2122) technology for higher yields and fewer fines", "Chain-Vey\u00ae tubular drag conveyors that move fragile products without degradation", "Turnkey process system integration covering classification, storage, transport, mixing, and automation", "24/7/365 virtual technical support with dedicated service engineers", "Global on-site service deployment on short notice"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1957 -> /about", "Family-owned business -> /about", "Headquarters in Chicago, USA -> /about, db", "Designs, manufactures and offers industrial process equipment -> /about", "World''s leading manufacturer of coffee grinding equipment -> /", "Gran-U-Lizer corrugated roller mill technology -> /, /about", "Chain-Vey tubular drag conveyors -> /, /about", "Process system design & integration -> /, /about", "SRM.MAX smallest roller-style coffee grinder -> /", "Serves coffee, food, chemical, mineral, distillery, pet food, powder/bulk solids -> /about", "Customers include Death Wish Coffee, Lawrence Foods, Westrock, Wicked Joe Coffee -> /, /about", "24/7/365 virtual technical support -> /services", "Global on-site service -> /services", "Exchange program for granulator heads/rolls -> /services", "Commissioning & startup support -> /services", "Operator & maintenance training -> /services", "Clean-in-place (CIP) conveyor systems -> /about", "Cable conveyor retrofit -> /about", "Pneumatic transport -> /about", "Coffee degassing -> /about", "Grind testing lab -> /about", "Pre-sale application analysis -> /services", "Spare parts supply -> /services", "French language support -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Founded in 1957 with worldwide headquarters in Chicago, USA, Modern Process Equipment Corporation, a family-owned business, has established a reputation for designing, manufacturing and offering unparalleled industrial process equipment and services.", "founded_year": "1957", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": ["English", "French"], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='modern-process-equipment-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Modula Inc. operates from Lewiston, Maine, where it was founded in 1991.

The product line centers on vertical lift modules such as the Modula Next, the high-throughput Modula Flexibox capable of processing up to 180 bins per hour, and the Modula Pallet for euro-pallet handling. Systems are built in the United States and sold through a network of more than 70 dealers across North America. The company reports more than 20,000 installations worldwide and 35-plus years of experience in warehouse automation.

Customers span aerospace, naval, biomedical, pharmaceutical, firearms, hospitality, automotive, e-commerce, electronics, food and beverage, and maritime sectors. Reference installations include Dassault Falcon Jet, GF Machining Solutions, Innomed, Rotor Clip, Symrise, Walser BMW, and Enercon Technologies.

