UPDATE companies SET description='Module Master was founded in 2004 by Gavin Curtis in Moscow, Idaho. The business began in a small pump house on his parents'' property and has since grown into a remanufacturing operation with two facilities in Moscow, home to the University of Idaho.

The company specializes in rebuilding automotive electronic modules, including ABS controllers, instrument clusters, climate control units, power accessory modules, and powertrain control modules. Its technicians perform component-level repair, partial testing, and full remanufacturing using an array of testing equipment and manufacturing machines. The shop processes more than 1,000 modules each month across its two locations.

Module Master serves the automotive and transportation sectors, covering cars, trucks, motorcycles, ATVs, UTVs, and RVs. Its customers range from individual vehicle owners to independent repair shops such as K‑Tech Automotive and ABS Automotive in San Mateo, California.

The company states that its remanufactured modules meet or exceed OEM quality at a fraction of the cost of new replacements, positioning the service as a sustainable alternative. It emphasizes a focus on detail, quality control, and ongoing customer support.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["ABS module rebuilding", "Instrument cluster rebuilding", "Climate control module rebuilding", "Power accessory module rebuilding", "Powertrain module rebuilding", "Partial testing of modules", "Component-level repair", "Electronic module remanufacturing"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Motorcycle", "ATV/UTV", "RV", "Commercial vehicle"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Over 1,000 modules per month", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Remanufactured modules meet or exceed OEM quality at a fraction of new replacement cost", "Component-level repair and testing using extensive in-house equipment", "Processes over 1,000 modules per month across two facilities", "Sustainable alternative to purchasing new electronics", "Focus on detail, quality control, and continued customer support"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2004 by Gavin Curtis -> /", "Located in Moscow, Idaho -> db, /", "Operates two facilities in Moscow, Idaho -> /", "Processes over 1,000 modules per month -> /", "Specializes in ABS, instrument cluster, climate control module rebuilding -> /", "Serves automotive, motorcycle, ATV/UTV, RV markets -> /", "Offers rebuild services for various module types -> /", "Rebuilds to higher quality than OEM at fraction of cost -> db", "7000 sq ft facility with testing equipment -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a team of electrical engineers and technicians who remanufacture automotive electronics.", "founded_year": "2004", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'