UPDATE companies SET description='Mohawk Electrical Systems, Inc. is headquartered in Milford, Delaware. The company was founded in 1963 by Clarence and Stephen Welch. In 1988, Scott Welch joined the firm and became the third-generation owner in 2006, continuing family ownership.

The company operates as a basic-to-complex assembly integrator, combining precision manufacturing with quality components to produce custom assemblies. Core capabilities include bridgewire and ordnance products, electromechanical assemblies, cable and harness assemblies, and contract manufacturing. Processes encompass multi-conductor instrument cable, coaxial cable, specialty power cables, multi-point harnesses, and molded rubber components for turnkey assemblies.

Mohawk serves the defense, oil and gas, pyrotechnics, instrumentation, mining, and construction industries. Its products are used in military applications such as the M18A1 and M68 Claymore weapon systems, as well as in commercial explosive products for coal mining, dam construction, roads, railways, and other large projects. The company also supports oil and gas well perforating and pyrotechnic systems.

Mohawk emphasizes a reputation for superior quality and reliability of detonators in military applications. Its quality assurance program includes receiving inspection of all materials, infrared and video inspection technology, statistical process control during production, 100% line and final product inspection, and packing and shipping inspection. The firm states that this integrated approach delivers improved product quality, on-time delivery, and overall customer satisfaction.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Bridgewire and ordnance products manufacturing", "Electromechanical assembly", "Cable and harness assembly", "Contract manufacturing", "Multi-conductor instrument cable fabrication", "Coaxial cable assembly", "Specialty power cable assembly", "Multi-point harness assembly", "Molded rubber components for turnkey assemblies", "Receiving inspection of materials and components", "Infrared and video inspection", "Statistical process control (SPC)", "100% line and final product inspection", "Packing and shipping inspection"], "industries": ["Defense", "Oil & Gas", "Pyrotechnics", "Instrumentation", "Mining", "Construction"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Reputation for superior quality and reliability of detonators in military applications", "Integrated manufacturing with in-house quality assurance programs", "100% line and final product inspection", "Infrared and video inspection technology", "Statistical process control monitoring"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1963 by Clarence and Stephen Welch -> db", "Scott Welch joined in 1988, became third-generation owner in 2006 -> db", "Headquartered in Milford, Delaware -> db", "ISO9001 certified -> db", "Produces bridgewire and ordnance products, electromechanical assemblies, cable and harness assemblies -> /", "Serves defense, oil & gas, pyrotechnics, instrumentation, mining, construction industries -> /", "Quality assurance includes receiving inspection, infrared/video inspections, SPC, 100% line and final inspection, packing/shipping inspection -> /quality", "Reputation for superior quality and reliability of detonators in military applications -> /", "M18A1 & M68 Claymore Weapon System -> /", "International representation expanding -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Basic to Complex Assembly Integrator ... combines precision manufacturing capabilities with quality components to produce custom, basic or multi-stage assemblies", "founded_year": "1963", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mohawk-electrical-systems-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Moldgenix operates from Trumbauersville, Pennsylvania. The company traces its roots to 1987, when the legacy of excellence and innovation was established.

The firm provides end-to-end contract manufacturing for plastic injection molding, including mold construction, micro-molding, tooling, automation, machining, and production. Its FDA-registered facility holds ISO 13485:2016 certification and offers clean room manufacturing compliant with the same standard. Secondary operations cover overmolding, laser marking, laser bonding, milling, welding, and ultrasonic welding, while assembly, kitting, and packaging services range from simple boxing to sealed medical packaging. The company handles both small-scale runs and full-scale production.

Moldgenix serves medical device OEMs, consumer product brands, personal care companies, and manufacturers in telecommunications, commercial, and high-end electronics markets. Its expertise spans Class I and II finished medical devices, jig and fixture construction, and finished goods packaging.

