UPDATE companies SET description='Molding Dynamics Inc. was founded in 2001 in Bedford, Ohio, a suburb of Cleveland. The company began as a specialist in plastic injection molding using engineering-grade resins and has grown through acquisition and facility consolidation.

Today the company operates a 40,000-square-foot manufacturing facility housing 22 injection molding presses ranging from 75‑ton to 700‑ton capacity, including vertical presses with shuttle tables for complex insert molding. Its core processes cover custom plastic injection molding, insert molding, and overmolding, supported by value‑added services such as assembly, sonic welding, pad printing, chrome plating, and tooling transfers. The shop handles projects from short‑run prototypes to high‑volume production runs.

Molding Dynamics serves customers in energy (coal, fracking, wind, solar), consumer goods, medical, construction, and general industrial markets. The firm emphasizes tight‑tolerance components for medical devices, durable parts for construction and energy applications, and visually appealing pieces for consumer products.

The company differentiates itself through ISO‑compliant quality systems, early collaboration on design for manufacturing and material selection, a skilled workforce trained in‑house, and a reshoring program that promises reduced lead times, lower logistics costs, and tariff‑free domestic production.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom plastic injection molding", "Insert molding", "Overmolding", "Design for Manufacturing (DFM)", "CAD modeling", "Rapid prototyping", "Engineering & project support", "Complete part assembly", "Tooling transfers", "Inventory control", "Sonic welding & heat staking", "Pad printing & decorating", "Metal plating & stamping", "Plastic, rubber & custom extrusion", "Reshoring services", "Material/resin selection", "Project management", "Chrome plating"], "industries": ["Energy", "Consumer Goods", "Medical", "Construction", "Industrial"], "materials": ["Acrylonitrile Butadiene Styrene (ABS)", "Acetal", "Acrylic", "Nylons", "Polyetheretherketone (PEEK)", "Cross-Linked Polyethylene (PEX)", "Polypropylene (PP)", "Polystyrene (PS)", "Polyethylene Terephthalate (PET)/Polybutylene Terephthalate (PBT)", "Polyurethane (PUR and PU)", "Polycarbonate (PC)", "Polyethylene (HDPE/LDPE/LLDPE)", "Polyphenylene Oxide (PPO)", "Thermoplastic Rubber (TPR)/Thermoplastic Elastomers (TPE)"], "equipment": ["22 injection molding presses (75\u2011ton to 700\u2011ton)", "Vertical presses with shuttle tables"], "volume": "Short-run to high-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO\u2011compliant quality management system", "40,000 sq ft facility with 22 presses (75\u2011ton to 700\u2011ton)", "Vertical presses with shuttle tables for complex insert molding", "Full range of engineering\u2011grade and commodity resins", "Reshoring program offering reduced lead times and zero tariffs"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2001 -> /", "Headquarters in Bedford, Ohio -> /", "40,000 sq ft facility -> /about-us", "22 injectio