UPDATE companies SET description='Montana Metal Fabrications, Inc. opened in Great Falls, Montana, on January 6, 2003. Founder Dean Brandt started the company to serve the state''s grain, fertilizer, feed, and seed elevator operators with repair, installation, and custom parts fabrication. In 2010 Phil Gates joined the crew, and when Brandt retired in 2026, Gates and his wife Laura became the owners.

The company runs a full fabrication shop equipped for shearing, braking, and rolling 1/4‑inch steel, plus hand plasma cutters and a bending/rolling machine added in 2009 for ornamental scrolls, baskets, and pickets. Core output includes elevator components such as spouting, conveyors, legs, and distributors; custom utility trailers, flatbeds, and truck boxes; water, waste‑oil, and fuel tanks (up to 100 gallons); and a range of decorative items from fire pits and benches to BBQ smokers and custom art. Welding and repair cover carbon steel, stainless steel, and aluminum.

Primary customers are agricultural operations — commercial and private grain elevators, fertilizer plants, and feed/seed facilities — throughout Montana. The shop also serves industrial clients needing tower installations, ladders, catwalks, and drilling‑rig accessories, as well as residential buyers seeking one‑off ornamental metalwork.

The founders’ original goal was to keep Montana’s agricultural infrastructure running with reliable, local service. Today the team emphasizes versatility: “if you can dream it, we can probably build it,” backing that claim with mobile repair crews and a shop that handles both heavy structural work and fine decorative detail.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Elevator parts fabrication (spouting, conveyors, legs, distributors)", "Custom steel fabrication per customer specifications", "Welding and fabrication of steel, stainless steel, and aluminum", "Custom utility trailers, flatbeds, and truck boxes", "Tank fabrication (water, waste oil, fuel up to 100 gallons)", "On\u2011site mobile repair and installation", "Shearing, braking, rolling 1/4\" steel", "Hand plasma cutting", "Bending/rolling for ornamental work", "Custom ornamental fabrication (benches, fire pits, planters, BBQ smokers, decorative art)", "Tower installation", "Ladder and catwalk fabrication"], "industries": ["Agriculture (grain, fertilizer, feed, seed handling)", "Industrial equipment repair and installation", "Custom metal fabrication for commercial and residential"], "materials": ["Steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum"], "equipment": ["Shearing machine", "Braking machine", "Rolling machine (1/4\" steel)", "Hand plasma machines", "Bending/rolling machine (for intricate baskets, scrolls, pickets)", "Mobile service units"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Mobile units for on\u2011site repairs, service, and installations across Montana", "Full fabrication shop with shearing, braking, and rolling 1/4\u2033 steel capacity", "Hand plasma cutting for custom ornamental work", "Bending/rolling machine for intricate scrolls, baskets, and pickets", "Custom fabrication from elevator components to decorative art"], "facts_used": ["Founded January 6, 2003 -> /about", "Headquarters Great Falls, Montana -> db", "Owners: Dean & Wendy Brandt (retired), Phil & Laura Gates (current) -> /about", "Services: elevator repair, parts fabrication, custom trailers, tanks, ornamental items -> /services", "Equipment: shearing, braking, rolling 1/4\" steel, hand plasma, bending/rolling machine -> /about", "Materials: steel, stainless steel, aluminum -> /services", "Industries: agricultural elevators, fertilizer plants, industrial, residential -> /services", "Mobile units for on-site service -> /about", "Company type: fabrication shop, custom fabrication -> /about, /services"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom steel fabrication per customer specifications", "founded_year": "2003", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='montana-metal-fabrications' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Montana Metal Works & Signs operates from Great Falls, Montana, as a locally owned and operated metal fabrication and welding shop serving Great Falls, Shelby, Fairfield, and the surrounding region. The company does not disclose a founding year or founder names, but presents itself as a direct-source fabricator with no subcontracting of metalwork.

The shop provides welding (including precision TIG for aluminum and stainless steel), custom metal fabrication, structural steel assemblies, CNC sign fabrication, sandblasting, and powder coating. All cutting, welding, and finishing are performed in-house using CNC cutting equipment, a powder coating system, and mobile welding rigs that allow on-site repairs across rural Montana. No facility size, headcount, or production volumes are published.

Customers span residential, commercial, and agricultural sectors. Examples include ranchers needing custom gates and urgent equipment repairs, commercial property owners requiring railings and structural steel, and homeowners seeking custom signage and decorative metalwork. The company notes that agricultural repairs often demand quick turnaround to minimize operational impact, while architectural pieces require attention to design detail and finish quality.

The business emphasizes accountability, follow-through, and direct communication with the welders and fabricators doing the work. Its differentiators include complete in-house control from design through finish, mobile welding that brings full capabilities to the field, and after-hours emergency service. The team cites familiarity with Montana’s temperature swings, weather exposure, and agricultural schedules as context that shapes their approach to durability and scheduling.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["TIG welding", "Aluminum welding", "Stainless steel welding", "Steel welding", "Custom metal fabrication", "Structural steel fabrication", "CNC cutting", "CNC sign fabrication", "Powder coating", "Sandblasting", "Mobile welding", "On-site welding", "Commercial welding", "Industrial welding", "Equipment repair", "Custom gates and railings fabrication"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Agricultural"], "materials": ["Steel", "Aluminum", "Stainless steel"], "equipment": ["CNC cutting system", "Powder coating system", "Mobile welding equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house CNC cutting, welding, and powder coating under one roof", "Mobile welding rigs for on-site repairs and installations", "Direct communication with fabricators\u2014no subcontracting", "After-hours emergency service available", "Experience with Montana\u2019s harsh weather and agricultural timing"], "facts_used": ["Located in Great Falls, MT -> /", "Serves residential, commercial, agricultural clients -> /", "Offers mobile on-site welding -> /", "In-house CNC cutting, welding, powder coating -> /about", "No subcontracting; direct work with fabricators -> /about", "After-hours emergency services -> /about", "Materials: steel, aluminum, stainless steel -> /", "Services: TIG welding, aluminum welding, stainless steel welding, custom fabrication, CNC sign fabrication, powder coating, sandblasting -> /", "Industries: residential, commercial, agricultural -> /about", "Equipment: CNC cutting system, powder coating system, mobile welding equipment -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Montana Metal Works & Signs is a locally operated metal fabrication and welding company serving Great Falls, Shelby, Fairfield, and surrounding areas.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='montana-metalworks-and-signs' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Montana Milling, Inc. operates grain mills in Conrad and Great Falls, Montana, in the heart of the state''s Golden Triangle wheat-growing region. The company was founded in 1972 and has served the baking industry for over five decades.

The company specializes in custom milling, cleaning, flaking, cracking, and blending of more than 20 whole grains. Its product line includes hard red spring and winter wheat, hard white wheat, soft white wheat, barley (whole, dehulled, pearled, malted, hulless waxy), buckwheat, oat groats, steel-cut oats, millet, corn, flax, rye, triticale, spelt, kamut, durum, and peas. A dedicated mix plant produces custom flour blends, flakes, cracks, and specialty mixes to customer specifications. Every shipment undergoes personal quality checks before leaving the mill.

Primary customers are commercial bakeries and food manufacturers that require consistent, high-quality grain ingredients. Montana Milling also works directly with growers and owner-operators in the Golden Triangle to source certified organic and conventional crops.

The company emphasizes its location in a grain-producing area, its ability to tailor milling and blending to exact specifications, and a quality guarantee that includes strict testing standards and individual shipment inspection.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom milling", "Grain cleaning", "Flaking (rolling)", "Cracking", "Blending", "Custom blend formulation", "Quality testing", "Organic processing", "Conventional processing"], "industries": ["Baking industry"], "materials": ["Hard Red Spring Wheat", "Hard Red Winter Wheat", "Hard White Wheat", "Soft White Wheat", "Whole Barley", "Dehulled Barley", "Pearled Barley", "Malted Barley", "Hulless Waxy Barley", "Buckwheat (Groats/Grits)", "Oat Groats", "Steel Cut Oat Groats", "Whole Millet", "Dehulled Millet", "Yellow Corn", "Blue Corn", "Brown Flax", "Golden Flax", "Rye", "Triticale", "Spelt", "Khorasan (Kamut\u00ae Brand Wheat)", "Durum", "Peas (Yellow and Green)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Mills located in Montana''s Golden Triangle grain region", "Custom milling and blending to customer specifications", "Over 20 whole grain varieties available", "Every shipment personally quality checked", "Certified organic and conventional product lines"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1972 -> db", "Headquarters Conrad, Montana -> db", "Two locations Great Falls and Conrad -> /", "Custom milling and blending -> /", "Over 20 whole grain varieties -> /", "Baking industry focus -> /", "Quality guarantee and personal shipment inspection -> /", "Certified organic and conventional products -> /", "Product list of specific grains -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We specialize in custom milling, meeting each customer''s special needs and demands.", "founded_year": "1972", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='montana-milling' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The Monterey Company operates from Bend, Oregon, where it has manufactured custom promotional products since 1989.

Minimum orders start at 25 pieces, with volume discounts on larger runs; the catalog lists thousands of SKUs.

Customers span the U.S. military (Army, Navy, Air Force, Marine Corps, National Guard), law enforcement, fire departments, corporate brands, and event organizers. Recent projects include challenge coins for the Indiana Army National Guard, custom belt buckles, embroidered patches for a firefighter apparel brand, and race medals for sporting events. The company also supplies nursing pins, letterman patches, and general promotional products such as apparel, magnets, and lanyards.

